<title>USA: U.S. AG Reno - states to take lead in tobacco suits. [CORRECTED 18:46 GMT]</title>
<headline>U.S. AG Reno - states to take lead in tobacco suits. [CORRECTED 18:46 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Attorney General Janet Reno said Wednesday the Justice Department was letting the states take the lead in suits against tobacco companies.</p>
<p>&quot;It was the states' cause of action. We want to work with the states,&quot; Reno said at a Senate Judiciary Committee hearing.</p>
<p>She was responding to a question by Sen. Edward Kennedy, D-Mass., on whether the federal government would join 24 (corrects from 22) states in suing tobacco companies to recover health costs in treating tobacco-related illnesses.</p>
</text>
